  "description": "Small, lucky, and fiercely home-loving folk. Their names are warm and familiar — usually with a family name attached.",
  "lore": "Halfling names are typically friendly, even whimsical — short syllables and open vowels. A halfling is almost always known by both a given name and a family name (the 'patronym' is the family, not the father). Family names are often cheerful, descriptive nicknames that became surnames: 'Goodbarrel', 'Tealeaf', 'Underbough'. Halfling women of the same family often share a name; the family name doesn't change with marriage.",
